 "_about": "Hand corrections for devout_life.py. Chapters are numbered from 0 in reading order. \"titles\": chapter titles, checked against the book's table of contents. \"first\": for each chapter, how many of the scan's opening words to replace, the right words, then pairs of [wrong, right] within the first paragraph (the ornamental initial of each chapter cannot be read by a scanner). \"words\": pairs of [wrong, right] for the rest of a chapter; each must match exactly once. Most put right what all three scans misread; a few correct the printer (such as \"devoton\", \"moral sin\" for \"mortal sin\", and the references Gen. xxviii and Ps. xciv, printed as xxxviii and xlv). \"join\": the opening words of a paragraph that belongs to the one before it. \"split\": words at which a paragraph should break. \"notes\": the edition's footnotes, lifted out of the paragraph the scans ran them into, as [start, end] stretches of text. \"lead\": a line shown under a chapter's title.",
 "titles": {
  "0": "Abstract of the life of St. Francis of Sales",
  "1": "A dedicatory prayer of the author",
  "2": "The author’s preface",
  "3": "The description of true devotion",
  "4": "The propriety and excellency of devotion",
  "5": "Devotion is compatible with every station of life",
  "6": "Of the necessity of a guide to conduct us in the way of devotion",
  "7": "That we must begin by purifying the soul",
  "8": "Of the first purgation, which is that of mortal sin",
  "9": "Of the second purgation, which is that of affection to sin",
